findings.recommendation:
Refactor each test to bind the store via the trait reference. Concrete pattern for `test_save_and_find_by_tx`:
```rust
let store = SqliteStore::in_memory().unwrap();
let attestations: &dyn AttestationStore = &store;
attestations.save_attestation("att-1", "content", ...).unwrap();
let found = attestations.find_by_tx("sol_tx_1").unwrap();
assert!(found.is_some());
```
Apply the same pattern to test_lineage_save_and_get and test_lineage_clear (cast to `&dyn LineageStore`). Add at least one new test that exercises BOTH trait references on the same store value to guarantee a single backend can satisfy both contracts simultaneously: `let store = SqliteStore::in_memory().unwrap(); let a: &dyn AttestationStore = &store; let l: &dyn LineageStore = &store; a.save_attestation(...); l.save_edge(...);`. Litmus test for the new tests: removing one of the trait impls (or making a method signature drift from the trait) must cause compile failure, not silent shadow-binding to the inherent impl.

Add to the top of `core/src/compress/mod.rs` (or in the inline tests module if the constant is test-only):
